# udev rules for the Redragon M711 Pro (Compx 25a7) — open-m711pro
#
# Installed by `open-m711pro setup` (or packaging/install.sh from a checkout).
# By hand: copy to /etc/udev/rules.d/99-m711pro.rules, then:
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
# (both installers do this for you)
#
# The mouse is configured through HID Feature Reports on its /dev/hidraw* node,
# which is root-only by default. These rules hand access to the logged-in user.
#
# WHY uaccess AND NOT MODE="0666"
#
#   MODE="0666" makes the raw HID node world-readable AND world-writable for
#   every account on the machine, permanently, whether or not anyone is sitting
#   at the keyboard. A hidraw node for a mouse is not a harmless file: anything
#   that can read it sees every button and movement the device reports, which is
#   an input-sniffing channel, and anything that can write it can reprogram the
#   device (this project remaps buttons to keystrokes — so a hostile writer can
#   turn a mouse button into an arbitrary key). On a multi-user box, or with any
#   sandboxed/daemon account, that is a real privilege leak.
#
#   TAG+="uaccess" is the modern systemd/logind mechanism: logind attaches an
#   ACL granting access to the user of the *currently active local session*, and
#   revokes it when that session ends or is switched away. Same convenience for
#   a normal desktop, far smaller blast radius, no world-writable device node.
#   This is what upstream projects (libratbag/piper, OpenRGB, solaar) settled on.
#
#   Requirement: systemd-logind (any mainstream desktop distro). If you are on a
#   system without logind, comment the two uaccess rules out and uncomment the
#   GROUP fallback at the bottom — it is still better than 0666 because access
#   is limited to members of one group.
#
# The device appears under two product IDs: fa07 is the 2.4G receiver (dongle),
# fa08 is the mouse itself over its own radio or over the cable. Both need the
# rule, because which one shows up depends on how the mouse is connected.

# 2.4G receiver (dongle)
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="25a7", ATTRS{idProduct}=="fa07", TAG+="uaccess"

# Mouse (own radio or USB cable)
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="25a7", ATTRS{idProduct}=="fa08", TAG+="uaccess"

# --- Fallback for systems without systemd-logind -----------------------------
# Comment out the two rules above and uncomment these, then add yourself to the
# group:  sudo usermod -aG plugdev $USER   (log out and back in)
#
#SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="25a7", ATTRS{idProduct}=="fa07", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660"
#SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="25a7", ATTRS{idProduct}=="fa08", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660"
